  "id": "cognitive-appraisal-theory",
  "term": "cognitive appraisal theory",
  "definition": "Cognitive appraisal theory is the idea that people’s responses to a demand depend on how they mentally evaluate it. In this source, it means that the same workplace technology requirement can be seen either as a challenge that supports positive action or as a hindrance that leads to avoidance and negative outcomes.",
